' Use case diagram for section 2 (2-use-case-diagram.md), part 2 of 3: procurement and accounts.
' The farm's use case diagram is split into three figures by stage of the batch
' (use-case-rearing, use-case-procurement, use-case-slaughter-sales); all use the identical boundary label.
' Rendered with Graphviz dot. Re-render after editing:
'   java -jar tools/plantuml.jar -tpng diagrams/use-case-procurement.puml   (needs Graphviz 'dot')
' Layout: all actors on the left; suppliers on the right scatters the lines.
' Suppliers are not linked to the Deliver use cases directly: each Order includes its Deliver, so the supplier
'   linked to the Order takes part in the delivery; direct links ran over the boundary title.
@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 14

actor "Director" as DIR
actor "Chick Supplier" as CSUP
actor "Feed Supplier" as FSUP
rectangle "Nurota Halol Parranda: current operations" {
  usecase "Order Day-Old Chicks" as OC
  usecase "Deliver Day-Old Chicks" as DC
  usecase "Order Feed and Vitamins" as OF
  usecase "Deliver Feed and Vitamins" as DF
  usecase "Pay Supplier at Batch End" as PY
  usecase "Calculate Batch Profit" as CP
  usecase "Record in pDaftar" as PD
}
DIR -- OC
DIR -- OF
DIR -- PY
DIR -- CP
PY ..> PD : <<include>>
OC ..> DC : <<include>>
OF ..> DF : <<include>>
CSUP -- OC
CSUP -- PY
FSUP -- OF
FSUP -- PY
@enduml
